The restriction is $x\ne2$. Multiply by $(x-2)^2$, which is positive for every permitted input.
$\begin{align*}x-2&>(x-2)^2\\0&>(x-2)^2-(x-2)\\(x-2)(x-3)&<0\end{align*}$
The quadratic is below the $x$-axis between its roots.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(4.3,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-0.7)--(0,2.6);
\path (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,2.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue,domain=0.9:4.1,samples=65] plot (\x,{(\x-2)*(\x-3)});
\path (2,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$2$} (3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$};
\path (2.6,2.6) node[above,text=curveBlue] {$y=(x-2)(x-3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Neither endpoint satisfies the strict inequality; $x=2$ is also excluded by the original denominator.
$2<x<3$.

The restriction is $x\ne3$. Multiply by $(x-3)^2>0$.
$\begin{align*}(x+2)(x-3)&\le2(x-3)^2\\0&\le2(x-3)^2-(x+2)(x-3)\\(x-3)(x-8)&\ge0\end{align*}$
The quadratic is on or above the $x$-axis for $x\le3$ or $x\ge8$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=2mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(10,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-8)--(0,12);
\path (10,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,12) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue,domain=1.5:9.5,samples=65] plot (\x,{(\x-3)*(\x-8)});
\path (3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$} (8,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$8$};
\path (5.5,12) node[above,text=curveBlue] {$y=(x-3)(x-8)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Exclude $x=3$; equality is permitted at $x=8$.
$x<3$ or $x\ge8$.

The restrictions are $x\ne2,-3$. Multiply by $(x-2)^2(x+3)^2>0$.
$\begin{align*}(x-2)(x+3)^2&>(x+3)(x-2)^2\\(x-2)(x+3)\bigl[(x+3)-(x-2)\bigr]&>0\\5(x-2)(x+3)&>0\\(x-2)(x+3)&>0\end{align*}$
The quadratic is above the $x$-axis outside its roots.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=2mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->,black] (-4.8,0)--(3.8,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-8)--(0,12);
\path (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,12) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue,domain=-4.5:3.5,samples=65] plot (\x,{(\x-2)*(\x+3)});
\path (-3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-3$} (2,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$2$};
\path (-4.8,22) node[anchor=south west,text=curveBlue] {$y=(x-2)(x+3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Both roots are excluded by the original denominators.
$x<-3$ or $x>2$.

The restriction is $x\ne0$. Multiply by $9x^2>0$.
$\begin{align*}9x&>x^3\\x^3-9x&<0\\x(x-3)(x+3)&<0\end{align*}$
The cubic has positive leading coefficient and roots $-3$, $0$ and $3$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=1.5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->,black] (-4.2,0)--(4.2,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-16)--(0,16);
\path (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,16) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue,domain=-3.6:3.6,samples=85] plot (\x,{\x*(\x-3)*(\x+3)});
\path (-3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-3$} (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$} (3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$};
\path (-4.2,30) node[anchor=south west,text=curveBlue] {$y=x(x-3)(x+3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The graph is below the $x$-axis for $x<-3$ or $0<x<3$. The strict inequality excludes the roots, including the undefined input $x=0$.
$x<-3$ or $0<x<3$.

The restriction is $x\ne1$. Multiply by $(x-1)^2>0$.
$\begin{align*}12(x-1)&\le x(x-1)^2\\0&\le x(x-1)^2-12(x-1)\\(x-1)(x^2-x-12)&\ge0\\(x-1)(x-4)(x+3)&\ge0\end{align*}$
The cubic has positive leading coefficient and roots $-3$, $1$ and $4$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=1mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->,black] (-4,0)--(5,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-20)--(0,25);
\path (5,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,25) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue,domain=-3.5:4.5,samples=85] plot (\x,{(\x-1)*(\x-4)*(\x+3)});
\path (-3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-3$} (1,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$1$} (4,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$4$};
\path (-4,46) node[anchor=south west,text=curveBlue] {$y=(x-1)(x-4)(x+3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The graph is on or above the $x$-axis for $-3\le x\le1$ or $x\ge4$. Exclude $x=1$ from the original denominator.
$-3\le x<1$ or $x\ge4$.
